Unit tests for this project

Run with:

    pio test -e native

This runs on your own machine, not the ESP32 - no flashing, no hardware
needed, seconds instead of minutes.

Why only some code is tested
-----------------------------
Almost everything in src/ talks directly to hardware (TFT_eSPI, Preferences/
NVS, analogRead, WiFi, LEDC), inline in the same functions as the actual
decision logic. That can't be unit tested without a lot of mocking, and
mocking a display/touchscreen/flash isn't worth it - the real thing gets
verified by actually running the device.

What's covered instead is logic that's easy to get subtly wrong and doesn't
need any hardware to check: given this input, is the output right? Each of
these lives in its own header/source pair with zero Arduino/ESP32 includes,
specifically so it can compile under `platform = native` in platformio.ini:

- AlarmLogic.h/.cpp - does a given alarm fire at a given moment (day-of-week,
  time-of-day, holiday skip, and the DST-hour correction)
- LdrHysteresis.h/.cpp - the backlight hysteresis/debounce decision
- WeatherIconShape.h/.cpp - weather condition string -> icon shape

Adding another one
-------------------
1. Pull the pure decision (no hardware calls) into its own .h/.cpp under
   include/ and src/, taking plain data in and returning plain data out.
2. Add it to the native env's build_src_filter in platformio.ini
   (+<YourFile.cpp>).
3. Add a test/test_<name>/test_<name>.cpp using Unity (see the existing
   suites for the pattern: setUp/tearDown, test_ functions, a main() that
   RUN_TESTs them).
4. The ESP32 build (env:esp32dev) picks up the new .cpp automatically -
   nothing to do there.
